{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789209152,"nonce":"sbXCfiblsInXVNrxkPNcL5nKRaM=","title":"Hot reload on the LLVM tier keeps calling the old body: calls are direct unless lazy_compilation","message":"crates/ash_interp/src/interpreter/mod.rs forces tier_mode = Llvm under hot_reload with the comment 'The LLVM tier already has an indirect-call rewrite for this'. It does not: the only producer of IndirectCall is air_emit.rs air_instr_opcode, gated on self.lazy_compilation (= compiled_only, i.e. --mode jit), and reload.rs recompiles a findex and patches functions_ptrs[findex] only. Under --mode hybrid --hot-reload every LLVM-compiled caller emits build_call(@Fun_N) and keeps the old body. The direct Call lowering should load the slot when hot_reload || lazy_compilation. Verify with scripts/test_hot_reload.sh.","files":null}]}